# A SofCat brand. Copy this directory to branding/<name>/ (gitignored) and
# build with `just brand=branding/<name> build` or `setup` (`build-macos` or
# `pkg` on a Mac). Every key is optional and falls back to stock SofCat, but
# SLUG, NAME and IDENTIFIER must all change together: the service, pipe,
# ProgramData folder, policy key, installer identity and launchd label derive
# from them.
# Values are sourced by bash.

# Service name, pipe prefix (<slug>-service), exe names (<slug>.exe,
# <slug>-ui.exe and <slug>-useragent.exe) and %LocalAppData% folder. 2-32 of
# a-z, 0-9 and -.
SLUG=acme-apps
# Display name: Start menu, Add/Remove Programs, window title, VERSIONINFO,
# C:\Program Files\<NAME>, C:\ProgramData\<NAME> and the branding policy key
# HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\<NAME>\Branding.
NAME="Acme Software Center"
# Reverse-DNS; the installer's package identifier and the macOS launchd label
# and bundle and package identifier, so keep it stable across releases.
IDENTIFIER=com.example.softwarecenter
PUBLISHER="Acme Corp"
DESCRIPTION="Install and update Acme-approved software"
HOMEPAGE=https://help.example.com/software
# Installer allowlist. Unset builds every installer type. "zip" builds the
# Windows binaries zip-only (the zip_only tag): no msi, exe, ps1, msix or nupkg
# installer is compiled in, and catalog items that need one are rejected. See site/src/content/docs/guides/zip-items.md#zip-only-builds.
#INSTALLERS=zip
